> Module Social_security

> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R

# Social Security benefits (Form 1040 lines 6a and 6b)

Direct File module `socialSecurity.xml`
(`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/socialSecurity.xml`,
"DF" below), scope.md section 3.5, issue #23. Tests:
`catala/tests/test_social_security.catala_en`. Oracle comparison:
`difftest/mappings/social_security.mjs` (`make difftest SCOPE=social_security`).

Inputs follow `catala/CONVENTIONS.md` section 3 (complete). The income
components of worksheet line 3 come from other modules (W-2, interest,
dividends, IRA, pensions, capital gains, other income); the orchestrator wires
them into this scope later, so they are plain inputs here.

Out of scope (knockouts, `catala/CONVENTIONS.md` section 6): the lump-sum
election (DF `/socialSecurityLumpSum` is hard-wired `False`; Pub. 915 "Lump-Sum
Election") and a net repayment over $3,000 (IRC 1341, DF
`/socialSecurityBenefitsAreLossGreaterThan3k`). The second one is reported by
the output `repayment_over_3k` so that the knockouts module can use it.

## 26 U.S.C. § 86

### (a) In general

"(1) ... gross income for the taxable year of any taxpayer described in
subsection (b) (notwithstanding section 207 of the Social Security Act)
includes social security benefits in an amount equal to the lesser of— (A)
one-half of the social security benefits received during the taxable year, or
(B) one-half of the excess described in subsection (b)(1)."
(`sources/statute/irc-86.html`)

"(2) ... the amount included in gross income under this section shall be equal
to the lesser of— (A) the sum of— (i) 85 percent of such excess, plus (ii) the
lesser of the amount determined under paragraph (1) or an amount equal to
one-half of the difference between the adjusted base amount and the base
amount of the taxpayer, or (B) 85 percent of the social security benefits
received during the taxable year."

### (b) Taxpayers to whom subsection (a) applies

"(1) A taxpayer is described in this subsection if— (A) the sum of— (i) the
modified adjusted gross income of the taxpayer for the taxable year, plus (ii)
one-half of the social security benefits received during the taxable year,
exceeds (B) the base amount." "(2) ... the term 'modified adjusted gross
income' means adjusted gross income— (A) determined without regard to this
section and sections 85(c), 135, 137, 221, 911, 931, and 933, and (B)
increased by the amount of interest received or accrued by the taxpayer during
the taxable year which is exempt from tax."

### (c) Base amount and adjusted base amount

"(1) ... the term 'base amount' means— (A) ... $25,000, (B) $32,000 in the
case of a joint return, and (C) zero in the case of a taxpayer who— (i) is
married as of the close of the taxable year (within the meaning of section
7703) but does not file a joint return for such year, and (ii) does not live
apart from his spouse at all times during the taxable year." "(2) ... the term
'adjusted base amount' means— (A) ... $34,000, (B) $44,000 in the case of a
joint return, and (C) zero in the case of a taxpayer described in paragraph
(1)(C)."

With base and adjusted base both zero, § 86(a)(2)(A) gives 85 percent of the
whole excess, capped by (B) at 85 percent of the benefits. The worksheet
shortcut is "multiply line 7 by 85%".

### (d) Social security benefit

"(2)(A) ... the amount of social security benefits received during any taxable
year shall be reduced by any repayment made by the taxpayer during the taxable
year of a social security benefit previously received by the taxpayer". This
is why net benefits (SSA-1099 / RRB-1099 box 5) can be negative.

## Form 1040 instructions: Social Security Benefits Worksheet, lines 6a and 6b

`sources/forms-instructions/i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 32. Pub. 915 has a similar
worksheet with different line numbers; DF uses the one in the 1040
instructions and so does this module. Lines:

- 1. "Enter the total amount from box 5 of all your Forms SSA-1099 and
  RRB-1099. Also enter this amount on Form 1040 or 1040-SR, line 6a."
- 2. "Multiply line 1 by 50% (0.50)".
- 3. "Combine the amounts from Form 1040 or 1040-SR, lines 1z, 2b, 3b, 4b, 5b,
  7, and 8".
- 4. "Enter the amount, if any, from Form 1040 or 1040-SR, line 2a".
- 5. "Combine lines 2, 3, and 4".
- 6. "Enter the total of the amounts from Schedule 1, lines 11 through 20, and
  23 and 25".
- 7. "Is the amount on line 6 less than the amount on line 5? No. None of your
  social security benefits are taxable. Enter -0- ... Yes. Subtract line 6
  from line 5".
- 8. "Married filing jointly, enter $32,000; Single, head of household,
  qualifying surviving spouse, or married filing separately and you lived
  apart from your spouse for all of 2024, enter $25,000; Married filing
  separately and you lived with your spouse at any time in 2024, skip lines 8
  through 15; multiply line 7 by 85% (0.85) and enter the result on line 16.
  Then, go to line 17".
- 9. "Is the amount on line 8 less than the amount on line 7? No. None of your
  social security benefits are taxable. Yes. Subtract line 8 from line 7".
- 10. "Enter $12,000 if married filing jointly; $9,000 if single, head of
  household, qualifying surviving spouse, or married filing separately and you
  lived apart from your spouse for all of 2024".
- 11. "Subtract line 10 from line 9. If zero or less, enter -0-".
- 12. "Enter the smaller of line 9 or line 10".
- 13. "Enter one-half of line 12".
- 14. "Enter the smaller of line 2 or line 13".
- 15. "Multiply line 11 by 85% (0.85). If line 11 is zero, enter -0-".
- 16. "Add lines 14 and 15".
- 17. "Multiply line 1 by 85% (0.85)".
- 18. "Taxable social security benefits. Enter the smaller of line 16 or line
  17. Also enter this amount on Form 1040 or 1040-SR, line 6b".

The "D" next to "benefits" on line 6a (MFS, lived apart all year) is the
output `benefit_code_d` (DF `/xmlSocialSecurityBenefitCode`).

## The scope

The worksheet rates are 50 percent and 85 percent (§ 86(a)(1) and (a)(2)).
They are declared here because only this module uses them.

```catala-metadata
## § 86(a)(1): one-half. Worksheet lines 2 and 13.
declaration ss_half content decimal equals 0.50

## § 86(a)(2): 85 percent. Worksheet lines 15, 16 (MFS shortcut) and 17.
declaration ss_eighty_five_percent content decimal equals 0.85

## Inputs and outputs of the worksheet. Names carry the worksheet line.
declaration scope SocialSecurity:
  # DF: /socialSecurityReports/*/netBenefits, one element per SSA-1099 or
  # RRB-1099 (box 5 of either form; negative when repayments exceed benefits)
  input report_net_benefits content list of money
  # DF: filingStatus module /isFilingStatusMFJ, /isFilingStatusMFS
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # DF: filers.xml /livedApartAllYear (only read for MFS)
  input lived_apart_all_year condition
  # DF: /employerIncomeSubtotal, 1040 line 1z
  input line_1z content money
  # DF: interest.xml /interestIncome, 1040 line 2b
  input line_2b content money
  # DF: interest.xml /taxExemptInterest, 1040 line 2a (worksheet line 4)
  input line_2a content money
  # DF: income.xml /ordinaryDividends, 1040 line 3b
  input line_3b content money
  # DF: income.xml /taxableIraDistributions, 1040 line 4b
  input line_4b content money
  # DF: income.xml /taxablePensionsAndAnnuities, 1040 line 5b
  input line_5b content money
  # DF: income.xml /capitalGainsOrLosses, 1040 line 7
  input line_7_capital_gains content money
  # DF: income.xml /otherIncome, 1040 line 8
  input line_8_other_income content money
  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /adjustmentsToIncomeExcludingStudentLoanInterest,
  # worksheet line 6 (Schedule 1 lines 11 to 20, 23, 25)
  input adjustments_excluding_student_loan_interest content money

  # DF: /socialSecurityBenefits, 1040 line 6a, worksheet line 1
  output line_6a content money
  # DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine3
  output wksht_line_3 content money
  # DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine7
  output wksht_line_7 content money
  # DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine8
  output wksht_line_8 content money
  # DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine9
  output wksht_line_9 content money
  # DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine10
  output wksht_line_10 content money
  # DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine11
  output wksht_line_11 content money
  # DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine16
  output wksht_line_16 content money
  # DF: /taxableSocialSecurityBenefits, 1040 line 6b, worksheet line 18
  output line_6b content money
  # DF: /nonTaxableSocialSecurityBenefits (Schedule R line 13a)
  output non_taxable_benefits content money
  # DF: /hasSocialSecurityBenefits
  output has_benefits condition
  # DF: /xmlSocialSecurityBenefitCode = "D"
  output benefit_code_d condition
  # DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsAreLossGreaterThan3k, without the screen-done flag
  output repayment_over_3k condition
```

## Line 1 and line 6a

DF `/socialSecurityBenefits` is `Round(sum of netBenefits)`.

```catala
scope SocialSecurity:
  # Worksheet line 1; DF: socialSecurity.xml /socialSecurityBenefits
  definition line_6a equals R.round_dollar of (Money.sum of report_net_benefits)

  # DF: /hasSocialSecurityBenefits
  definition has_benefits equals line_6a > $0

  # DF: /xmlSocialSecurityBenefitCode (case 1, the only case)
  definition benefit_code_d equals
    has_benefits and filing_status = MarriedFilingSeparately and lived_apart_all_year

  # IRC 1341(a)(3) via P.claim_of_right_threshold; DF: ...AreLossGreaterThan3k
  definition repayment_over_3k equals line_6a < - P.claim_of_right_threshold
```

## Lines 3 to 7

```catala
scope SocialSecurity:
  # Worksheet line 3; DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine3. No rounding in DF:
  # each addend is already a whole-dollar figure.
  definition wksht_line_3 equals
    line_1z + line_2b + line_3b + line_4b + line_5b
    + line_7_capital_gains + line_8_other_income

  # Worksheet lines 2 to 7, DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine7. Line 5 =
  # 0.50 * line 1 + line 3 + line 4 (2a); line 6 is the adjustments. "If line
  # 6 is not less than line 5, enter -0-" is `GreaterOf(..., 0)`. DF does not
  # round the 50% product to the dollar (it is rounded to the cent), only
  # the final line 18.
  definition wksht_line_7 equals
    Money.positive of
      ((line_6a * ss_half) + wksht_line_3 + line_2a
       - adjustments_excluding_student_loan_interest)
```

## Lines 8 to 16

Line 8 is the § 86(c)(1) base amount: $32,000 for a joint return, else
$25,000. The case "MFS and lived with spouse" (base amount zero, § 86(c)(1)(C))
is handled in line 16, as the worksheet does ("skip lines 8 through 15"). The
DF fact for line 8 does not look at it, so neither does `wksht_line_8`.

```catala
scope SocialSecurity:
  # Worksheet line 8; DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine8
  definition wksht_line_8 equals
    if filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly
    then P.ss_base_amount_joint
    else P.ss_base_amount_other

  # Worksheet line 9; DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine9 (may be negative;
  # DF only uses it after the line-9 early return)
  definition wksht_line_9 equals wksht_line_7 - wksht_line_8

  # Worksheet line 10; DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine10
  definition wksht_line_10 equals
    if filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly
    then P.ss_adjusted_base_gap_joint
    else P.ss_adjusted_base_gap_other

  # Worksheet line 11; DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine11
  definition wksht_line_11 equals
    Money.positive of (wksht_line_9 - wksht_line_10)

  # Worksheet lines 8 (MFS shortcut), 9 (early return), 12 to 16;
  # DF: /socialSecurityBenefitsWkshtLine16. Case order is DF's.
  definition wksht_line_16 equals
    if filing_status = MarriedFilingSeparately and not lived_apart_all_year
    then wksht_line_7 * ss_eighty_five_percent
    else if wksht_line_7 < wksht_line_8
    then $0
    else
      # line 15 + line 14, where line 14 = min(line 2, 0.50 * line 12)
      (wksht_line_11 * ss_eighty_five_percent)
      + Money.min of
          (line_6a * ss_half),
          ((Money.min of wksht_line_9, wksht_line_10) * ss_half)
```

## Lines 17 and 18

```catala
scope SocialSecurity:
  # Worksheet lines 17 and 18; DF: /taxableSocialSecurityBenefits. Net
  # benefits below zero give zero; otherwise Round(min(line 16, 0.85 * line 1)).
  definition line_6b equals
    if line_6a < $0
    then $0
    else R.round_dollar of
      (Money.min of wksht_line_16, (line_6a * ss_eighty_five_percent))

  # DF: /nonTaxableSocialSecurityBenefits = benefits - taxable benefits
  definition non_taxable_benefits equals line_6a - line_6b
```
